documentation style
===================

These rules apply to README and every file in docs/.  They exist to
keep the documentation short and readable.


Rules
-----

  * Imperative mood, active voice.  No filler openers.
  * One idea per paragraph; no paragraph longer than six lines.
  * Short lists or tables instead of bullet walls.  No nested bullets.
  * No marketing words.
  * Sentence case headings, underlined to match heading length.
  * Code in fenced blocks when multi-line; backticks for symbols and
    paths inline.
  * Do not restate a previous section; link to it.
  * Keep technical facts exact: flags, paths, symbol names, limits.


Checks
------

  * Lines no wider than 72 columns.
  * Spellcheck before committing.
  * Cross-reference every new file from docs/README.